Subject: [PATCH] power: refresh keyboard backlight capabilities after hotplug

UPower 1.91 updates its legacy keyboard backlight interface as LED devices
are added and removed. The cached maximum brightness otherwise leaves the
keyboard control visible after removal and misses a keyboard added later.

Reuse the existing UPower device notifications and legacy methods to read
capabilities asynchronously. Cancel superseded replies, publish unavailable
backlights as Brightness=-1 and Steps=0, and preserve the device brightness.
Capability changes do not report a hardware brightness key event.

The original legacy interface remains supported; no device-specific path
or new UPower keyboard enumeration API is required.

Origin: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-settings-daemon/-/blob/50.1/plugins/power/gsd-power-manager.c
